{"name":"String Deep","hex":"#7f7860","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"string","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, thin and flexible structure made from threads twisted together.","Control; influence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put (items) on a string.","To put strings on (something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/string"},{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"}],"entries":[{"title":"String","blocks":[{"text":"String is a long flexible tool made from fibers twisted together into a single strand, or from multiple such strands which are in turn twisted together. String is used to tie, bind, or hang other objects. It is also used as a material to make things, such as textiles, and in arts and crafts. String is a simple tool, and its use by humans is known to have been developed tens of thousands of years ago. String may also be a component in other tools, and in devices as diverse as weapons, musical instruments, and toys. The ubiquity of string as a tool has led to conceptual and scientific uses of the term, including strings in computer science, cosmic strings, and string theory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Length_of_string.jpg/330px-Length_of_string.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/String","wikidata":"Q11064354"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/